Perfect! I can see your CSV has columns for ID, Name, Department, and Salary. Let me provide you with a set of command-line tools to handle the migration processing:

## 1. First, let's check for basic file integrity and structure:```{bash}
# Count total records (excluding header)
wc -l /home/user/data/employee_records.csv

# Check for lines with wrong number of fields (should be 4 fields)
awk -F',' 'NF != 4 && NR > 1' /home/user/data/employee_records.csv

# Look for empty or malformed fields
awk -F',' 'NR > 1 && ($1 == "" || $2 == "" || $3 == "" || $4 == "")' /home/user/data/employee_records.csv
```

## 2. Validate and extract clean records:```{bash}
# Create a clean file with only valid records
awk -F',' '
  NR == 1 {print; next}  # Print header
  NF == 4 && $1 != "" && $2 != "" && $3 != "" && $4 != "" && $4 ~ /^[0-9]+$/ {print}
' /home/user/data/employee_records.csv > /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv

# Count records that were filtered out
echo "Original records:" $(wc -l < /home/user/data/employee_records.csv)
echo "Clean records:" $(wc -l < /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv)
echo "Filtered out:" $(( $(wc -l < /home/user/data/employee_records.csv) - $(wc -l < /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv) ))
```

## 3. Sort by Department (alphabetically):```{bash}
# Sort by department (skip header, then sort, then reattach header)
(head -1 /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv && tail -n +2 /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv | sort -t',' -k3) > /home/user/data/employee_records_by_dept.csv
```

## 4. Salary analysis and validation:```{bash}
# Extract salary statistics
echo "Salary Statistics:"
echo "=================="
awk -F',' 'NR > 1 {sum+=$4; count++} END {print "Average Salary: $" sum/count}' /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv
awk -F',' 'NR > 1 {if($4 > max) max=$4; if(min == "" || $4 < min) min=$4} END {print "Min Salary: $" min; print "Max Salary: $" max}' /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv

# Find potential outliers (salaries > 2 standard deviations)
awk -F',' '
  BEGIN {OFS=","}
  NR > 1 {
    sum+=$4; 
    sqsum+=$4*$4; 
    count++
  } 
  END {
    avg=sum/count
    stddev=sqrt(sqsum/count - avg*avg)
    print "Mean:" avg ",StdDev:" stddev ",Threshold (>2std):" avg+2*stddev
  }
' /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv

# List actual outliers
awk -F',' '
  NR > 1 {salaries[NR]=$4; lines[NR]=$0}
  END {
    # Calculate mean and stddev
    for(i=2; i<=NR; i++) {
      sum+=salaries[i]
      sqsum+=salaries[i]*salaries[i]
    }
    count=NR-1
    avg=sum/count
    stddev=sqrt(sqsum/count - avg*avg)
    threshold=avg+2*stddev

    print "Outliers (salary > $" int(threshold) "):"
    for(i=2; i<=NR; i++) {
      if(salaries[i] > threshold) print lines[i]
    }
  }
' /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv
```

## 5. Department-wise summary:```{bash}
# Count employees and average salary by department
echo -e "\\nDepartment Summary:"
echo "=================="
awk -F',' '
  NR > 1 {
    dept_count[$3]++
    dept_salary[$3]+=$4
  } 
  END {
    for(dept in dept_count) {
      printf "%-15s Count: %3d  Avg Salary: $%8d\\n", dept, dept_count[dept], dept_salary[dept]/dept_count[dept]
    }
  }
' /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv | sort
```

## 6. Final migration-ready output:```{bash}
# Create a final clean, sorted file ready for migration
(head -1 /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv && tail -n +2 /home/user/data/employee_records_clean.csv | sort -t',' -k1n) > /home/user/data/employee_records_final_migration.csv

echo -e "\\nFinal migration file created: employee_records_final_migration.csv"
echo "Records ready for migration:" $(tail -n +2 /home/user/data/employee_records_final_migration.csv | wc -l)
```

